  "agent": {
    "note": "master — @m0saic/alpine/timeline/v1 (the 8th Alpine template), LOCKED 2026-06-23. A milestone timeline in the friendly white card: a spine with a dot per event that draws down/across as events cascade in, each a date + title + description. ASPECT-AWARE: orientation 'auto' lays out a VERTICAL left-rail on square/tall cards and a HORIZONTAL spine (events alternating above/below) on wide cards so the layout always fills its canvas (or force vertical/horizontal). Built on the donut/heatmap absolute-placement model (tight rects on the 4px lattice, grid passed as a full-canvas extraLayer → no quantization). Three bugs fixed in the sandbox: (1) c001 wide-card empty width → added the orientation prop + horizontal layout; (2) horizontal edge events' centered text spilled past the card → clamp the block center in-bounds; (3) absurdly long titles overflowed + collided → truncate with an ellipsis bounded to one column. Per-event dot colors + custom accent; same dual props (Animate / Intro length / Show description). 6 stress variants approved (A dark · B forced-vertical+colors · C 7-events-no-desc · D square-static · E long-text · F overflow-truncation). Also shipped alongside: the `open --make` file-size passthrough so a square candidate opens at its authored aspect.",
    "question": "Locked master — showcase props (5-event MILESTONES timeline, auto orientation → horizontal at 1280x800, draw-down cascade). This is the preview the Templates page renders.",
    "response": {
      "body": "Approved — locked.",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z"
    }
  },
